WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.520
Dear Governor Ivey.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:02.860
My name is Michael Everette.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.200
I'm a retired lieutenant from the Alabama
Department of Corrections, Holman Prison.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.730
My name is Keith Watson.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.600
I worked for Alabama Department of
Corrections for 21 years.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.040
My name is Ernest Stanton, retired
correctional officer.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.480
For around 20 years or so.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.420
I worked on Death Row most of my time.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.260
My name is Freddie Howard.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.200
I'm a retired correctional officer.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:29.740
I'm a community person now, I teach Sunday
School, I'm a person that cares about God.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.360
My name is William James, I'm conservative, I
support law enforcement, and I support

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.550
law and order.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.120
Mark is a man who deserves to be saved.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.580
I think Mark Jenkins is a good person and
I do not think Mark should be executed.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:51.040
Mark brings an atmosphere of peace to a
very,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.520
very violent world.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.600
I consider him as a model inmate, and I
believe if he was given a second chance,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.210
he'll be a model person.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.660
When things are going crazy and haywire, Mark will
be a voice of reason in any turbulent

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:06.840
situation.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.800
I was the first officer to hire Mark as a
hall runner.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.000
We had to have a lot of trust in hall runners
because they had more time out of their

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.460
cells than the other inmates.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.030
Mark earned my trust.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.600
I do not take executions lightly.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.780
And I am asking Governor Ivey to grant clemency
for inmate Mark Jenkins on death row.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.680
So I can only say, I hope that he gets the
best come out for him.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.820
Governor, I voted for you and have
supported your tenure.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:39.220
You've said you care about the voices of
correctional officers and that you have our

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.410
back.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.580
I'm asking you to look at these letters.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:48.020
The officers that I work with at Holman, the
officers who have signed these letters of

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.600
support, they know Mark.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:55.000
They know and I know Mark deserves to have
his sentence commuted.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.540
God gives us a chance every day.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.410
You got up this morning.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.770
I got up this morning.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.960
He could have took us last night.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.840
He could have took us on our way here.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.800
But he gave you another chance.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.360
That says to you, there's more work for you
to do.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.200
That God is awesome and is in control.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:18.790
And he's a God of love.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.280
And love covers a multitude of sins.
